Remove Live Translate from chrome://settings/accessibility.

Live Translate is the machine-translation layer on top of Live Caption: it
sends recognised caption text to Google's translation backend. ungoogled-
chromium already neuters translation (core/ungoogled-chromium/
toggle-translation-via-switch.patch disables it unless the
--translate-script-url switch is passed) and Aerium already drops the
"Google Translate" card from chrome://settings/languages, so the toggle is
dead UI for a service the browser never talks to.

Contrary to what its name suggests, the section does not live in
a11y_page.html in Chromium 151 - it is the standalone
<settings-live-translate> element, instantiated from live_caption.html
behind the enableLiveTranslate_ flag. That is the only instantiation of it
anywhere in the settings bundle, so removing it plus the property that
gates it plus the module import takes the whole subsection (master toggle
and target-language dropdown) out of both places
<settings-live-caption> appears: inlined on
chrome://settings/accessibility (Windows, macOS) and on the
chrome://settings/captions subpage (Linux).

live_translate.ts is dropped from web_component_files so it stops being
compiled into the bundle at all. Taking it out of the build set is what
forces the lazy_load.ts change too: ts_library type-checks the whole
settings project in one tsc invocation, and lazy_load.ts re-exports
SettingsLiveTranslateElement from './a11y_page/live_translate.js'. Once
that specifier is no longer among the preprocessed in_files, the re-export
cannot resolve and //chrome/browser/resources/settings:build_ts fails with
"error TS2307: Cannot find module './a11y_page/live_translate.js'". So the
barrel entry has to go with it. lazy_load.ts is the export surface the
WebUI browser tests import through, not something the shipped bundle
reads, so dropping the one line has no runtime effect.

This is the one point where this patch goes further than
aerium-remove-translate-settings.patch: that patch deliberately leaves
translate_page.ts in web_component_files, which is why its own
lazy_load.ts export (SettingsTranslatePageElement) stays resolvable and
needs no matching hunk.

The source files themselves are left in the tree unreferenced, the same
way this series leaves translate_page.* after
aerium-remove-translate-settings.patch - deleting sources from a patch
buys nothing once nothing builds them, and keeps the patch trivially
reversible on a Chromium rebase.

The Live Translate loadTimeData strings (captionsEnableLiveTranslate*,
captionsLiveTranslateTargetLanguage*) and the enableLiveTranslate boolean
are deliberately left registered. They are inert data once nothing reads
them, and they are emitted from the *shared* captions strings provider that
also feeds the Live Caption UI we keep, so stripping them there would risk
the captions subpage for no user-visible gain.

# Rebased onto Chromium 152, where the settings pages this touches moved from
# Polymer to Lit. live_caption.html is now live_caption.html.ts and the
# dom-if wrapper around <settings-live-translate> is a template literal, so the
# element is removed from the new file rather than re-anchored in the old one.
# The BUILD.gn entries moved with it: live_translate's .ts and generated
# .html.ts belong to ts_files now instead of web_component_files, and its .css
# is listed separately again, so all three come out.

--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/BUILD.gn
@@ -394,8 +394,6 @@ build_webui("build") {
     ts_files += [
       "a11y_page/live_caption.html.ts",
       "a11y_page/live_caption.ts",
-      "a11y_page/live_translate.html.ts",
-      "a11y_page/live_translate.ts",
       "default_browser_page/default_browser_browser_proxy.ts",
       "default_browser_page/default_browser_page.html.ts",
       "default_browser_page/default_browser_page.ts",
@@ -456,7 +454,6 @@ build_webui("build") {
     "a11y_page/a11y_page_index.css",
     "a11y_page/captions_page.css",
     "a11y_page/live_caption.css",
-    "a11y_page/live_translate.css",
     "about_page/about_page.css",
     "appearance_page/appearance_fonts_page.css",
     "appearance_page/appearance_page.css",
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/a11y_page/live_caption.html.ts
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/a11y_page/live_caption.html.ts
@@ -77,9 +77,6 @@ ${this.enableLiveCaptionMultiLanguage_ ? html`
